.TH DILL 1 "February 2026" "0.0.1-alpha" "Dill Manual"
.SH NAME
dill \- A raunchy Aussie AUR helper for Arch-based Linux distros.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dill
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dill
is a modular, humorous, and raunchy update utility and AUR helper designed for Pickles Linux. 
It aims to be a complete replacement for other AUR helpers like Paru or Yay, providing a 
raunchy Aussie experience while keeping your system up to date.
.PP
It's rated R for Raunchy Aussie. If you're easily offended, you're probably a 🥒.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B update, -Syu [mirrors]
Syncs official repositories, updates official packages, and then checks and updates 
all AUR packages. If 'mirrors' is provided, it will also update your pacman mirrorlist 
using \fBrate-mirrors\fR.
.TP
.B install, -S <packages>
Attempts to install the specified packages. It first searches the official repositories 
and, if not found, searches the AUR. It handles building and installing AUR packages 
automatically.
.TP
.B remove, -R <packages>
Removes the specified packages from your system using \fBpacman -Rns\fR. It asks for 
confirmation before doing anything drastic.
.TP
.B search, query, -Q <query>
Searches for packages in the locally installed database, official repositories, and the AUR. 
It provides an interactive menu to install, remove, or view more information about the results.
.TP
.B help, -h, --help
Shows the help message. Use it if you're a drongo and forgot how to use the tool.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --mirror, --mirrors, --m
When used with the \fBupdate\fR command, triggers a mirrorlist update before syncing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dill/dill.config
User-specific configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dill/config/dill.config
System-wide default configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dill/config/dill.language
The language file containing all the raunchy Aussie messages. Edit this if you want 
to customize the humor or localize it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEBUG
If set to 'true' in the config, \fBdill\fR will output extra debugging information 
prefixed with ':>>'.
.SH AUTHOR
Stu Pickles <https://github.com/Stu-Pickles3047> for Pickles Linux.
